$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=z5dbern  LOC_AFTER=?

* Bernoulli's inequality for exponents in [ 0 , 1 ]: A ^ X <_ 1 + X ( A - 1 ) for A >_ 1 (the convexity of exp, set.mm's efcvx, at the endpoints 0 and log A).  It bounds the real part of the Euler-product factor of Gamma.

